# A quieter place to think

Welcome to **Hypertextual**. A local vault, plain files, and room for ideas to connect.

Move through the whole note with the keyboard. Headings and formatting stay rich while you type. A heading shows its Markdown marker beside the text when the cursor is inside it. **⌘ S** saves the note.

## Files first

- Notes live in `.htmd` files.
- Existing `.md` files open in the same editor.
- Folders give your vault a familiar shape.
- One note at a time. No tabs to manage.

> HTMD adds typed custom nodes to Markdown. Open **Examples/Chart** to see a live chart, its JSON data, and the exact file syntax. Notebook execution and database views are future work.

## A small example

```rust
let thought = "Keep the fast path simple.";
println!("{thought}");
```

| Format | Purpose | This experiment |
| --- | --- | --- |
| htmd | Notes | Editable |
| md | Existing Markdown | Editable |
| nbmd | Notebooks | Future |
| dbmd | Tables and databases | Future |

Try the notes in **Ideas** and **Reference** from the sidebar.

